From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Per-channel sound and music

Lets the host place sounds in space instead of hearing SM64's stereo mix
(src/audio/ar_audio_hooks.h). Inert unless gArMode and the host's flags.

- spatial SFX: notes of point-source SFX channels are mixed at centre gain
  into per-channel mono accumulators instead of the stereo mix, and those
  channels lose SM64's pan, distance volume loss and pitch rise; the host
  reads each channel's sound, bank and listener-space vector and spatializes
  it. The reverb send can keep vanilla's distance term (gArReverbOriginal).
- music: the level sequence's channels, and the environment player's
  channels while an event song plays, can be split per channel the same
  way; their reverb send stays in the stereo bed.
- every note keeps its channel tag whenever gArMode, so switching sound
  mode live does not lose notes already playing.

The host reads the accumulators once per tick after buffer_audio() and then
calls ar_sfx_tick_reset(). All globals are written on the game thread only.
---
